# NGA notes site

Jekyll GitHub Pages site. Readers consume compiled notes; maintainers file raw material as sources and cite it.

## Layers

| Layer | Path | Role |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Inbox | `inbox/` | Drop zone only — never publish |
| Sources | `_sources/*.md` + `assets/sources/<id>/` | Raw as received + author |
| Sessions | `_sessions/*.md` | Compiled notes per lesson |
| Places | `_places/*.md` | Compiled notes per curriculum stop |
| Program data | `_data/program.yml` | Schedule, `places:` links per session |

## Rules

- Preserve originals in sources; for photos/scans/PDFs write `assets/sources/<id>/transcription.md` before compiling.
- Synthesise on session/place pages; cite with `{% include cite.html id="source-id" %}`.
- Public pages: no maintainer how-tos or cite instructions.
- Do not invent facts; if material is unclear, file the source and note uncertainty in compiled text.
- New curriculum↔session links: update `places:` on the session in `_data/program.yml`.
- `baseurl` is `/nga-2026-notes` for production; local Docker serve uses `--baseurl ""`.

## Inbox

When `inbox/` has files (besides `README.md`), or the user asks to process notes/material: read and follow `.cursor/skills/process-inbox/SKILL.md`.
